processes or services and talks to them over sockets, HTTP or the command
line. It does not link them into Vaultcast.
  PHP 8.3 (NTS, x64)                           PHP License 3.01
  Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable         Microsoft Software License Terms
  Node.js LTS                                  MIT (bundled parts under their own licences)
  MariaDB Server 11.4                          GPL-2.0
  nginx                                        BSD-2-Clause
  FFmpeg "essentials" build (gyan.dev)         GPL-3.0 (GPL build: includes libx264/x265)
  Transmission (extracted from the MSI)        GPL-2.0 / GPL-3.0 (some parts MIT)
  WinSW 2.12                                   MIT
  curl CA bundle (cacert.pem, from Mozilla)    MPL-2.0
  NSIS installer stub and plugins              zlib/libpng
  Netplay npm packages                         see section 1

Licence texts: the installer installs every component's full licence text into
the "licenses" folder of the installation (licenses\INDEX.txt lists them). Where a
package ships its own licence files, build.ps1 takes them from that exact
package. Otherwise it uses the committed copies in Installers/Windows/NSIS/licenses.
The multiplayer relay's npm packages are listed with their licence files in
